WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Lahore, 1606.

2
00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:06.690
Guru Arjan, the fifth Guru,
dies in Mughal custody.

3
00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.900
Guru Nanak's path had been
peaceful and devotional:

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.100
hymns, meditation, honest work.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:18.800
Now the new Guru, Hargobind, takes his
place wearing not one sword, but two.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.750
He also builds a throne
facing the Harmandir Sahib,

7
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.430
where Sikhs worship.

8
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.750
So why would a Guru from a tradition of
peace and meditation start wearing two

9
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.050
swords?

10
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:33.450
In this mission, you'll meet the
ideal Sikhs call the saint-soldier.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.400
Then you'll find out why many Sikhs
still carry a small sword today,

12
00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.700
and what it is meant to remind them of.

13
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:45.010
Your mission: find out why a Guru of
peace and meditation took up two swords.
